.TH BFC 1 "2026-09-25" "bfc" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bfc \- compile Brainfuck source files to native executables
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bfc
.I source.bf
.RB [ \-o
.IR output ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bfc
compiles a Brainfuck source file into a native executable using Clang. The
source uses the eight standard Brainfuck commands. The
.B !
runtime-call extension is described in
.BR bfc-runtime (7).
.PP
If
.B \-o
is omitted, the executable is named
.BR a.out .
The generated program reads from standard input and writes to standard output
unless its source uses runtime calls to select other streams.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " output"
Write the executable to
.IR output .
The default is
.BR a.out .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CLANG
Name of the Clang executable used to link the generated program. The default
is
.BR clang .
.SH EXIT STATUS
The compiler exits with status 2 when no source file is given. A successful
compilation exits with status 0; file and linking errors produce a nonzero
status.
.SH EXAMPLES
Compile
.I hello.bf
to an executable named
.IR hello :
.PP
.RS
.B bfc hello.bf \-o hello
.br
.B ./hello
.RE
.PP
Compile to the default output name:
.PP
.RS
.B bfc hello.bf
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bfc-runtime (7),
.BR clang (1)
